# Phase 2 parity: node tell, node ask, node inbox. Each line runs on a fresh seeded home.
# A seeded home has no run, so these cases cover usage and unknown-run errors. The delivery path
# (seeded run with a node) is covered by skills/orch/tests/unit/inbox-core.test.sh.
# Not a case: `node ask` with no arguments. bash dies with "args[@]: unbound variable" (exit 1);
# the Bun path prints usage (exit 2). Bash bug, see the handoff.
node tell
node tell nope n1
node tell nope n1 hello
node tell nope n1 hello --from orch
node ask nope n1 question
node ask nope n1 question --wait --timeout 0
node ask nope n1 question --timeout x
node inbox
node inbox nope n1
node inbox nope n1 --json
node inbox nope n1 --peek
node inbox nope n1 --ack m1
node answer
node answer nope n1 hello
node cancel
node cancel nope n1
run messages
run messages nope
run broadcast
run broadcast nope hello
run rule
run rule add nope hello
run rule list nope
run repoint
run repoint nope /tmp/s p1
run pause
run pause nope
run resume
run resume nope
run stop
run stop nope
run set
run set nope auto_dispatch maybe
run set nope coordinator
run health
run health nope
run health nope --json
run guard nope
